<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan electronics shares rise on sales prospects.</title>
<headline>Taiwan electronics shares rise on sales prospects.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's electronics shares rose by mid-morning on Tuesday on expectations of sound profit and sales performances in August, brokers said.</p>
<p>With 70 minutes of trade left, the electronics sector was up 0.89 percent while the overall index had risen 0.18 percent.  </p>
<p>Synnex Technology surged T$3 or 4.55 percent to T$69 and Accton rose T$1.5 or 2.8 percent to T$55.</p>
<p>&quot;Many analysts expect good sales and profit performances in August by electronics, to be released in early September, because of the traditional hot-sale season in the third quarter,&quot; said Alex Yang of National Securities.</p>
<p>--Taipei Newsroom (5080815)</p>
</text>
